WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.375
Step 3 reads every check
on the file server.

2
00:00:03.375 --> 00:00:06.997
A server gets the two server
checks the workstations don't:

3
00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:10.468
network protection allowed
on the server, which passes,

4
00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:13.863
and datagram processing for
its file role, which fails.

5
00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:15.742
Step 4 reads the week's events:

6
00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:20.362
network protection audited twelve
times on four devices, three blocks,

7
00:00:20.362 --> 00:00:25.138
controlled folder access audited and
blocked, and one tampering attempt.

8
00:00:25.138 --> 00:00:28.550
The security operations center
reads that with the drift list.

9
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.667
A device with tamper
protection off and a tampering

10
00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.780
attempt in the same week is
an incident, not a ticket.
